# [Count Days Spent Together](https://leetcode.com/problems/count-days-spent-together/)

## Approach
- Extract the month and day from each arrival and departure date.
- Find the overlapping start date by taking the later arrival date.
- Find the overlapping end date by taking the earlier departure date.
- If the start date is after the end date, return `0`.
- Count the overlapping days month by month, including both the start and end dates.

## Code
```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int countDaysTogether(string arriveAlice, string leaveAlice, string arriveBob, string leaveBob) {
        int alice_arrived_month = stoi(arriveAlice.substr(0, 2));
        int alice_arrived_day = stoi(arriveAlice.substr(3, 2));
        int alice_leave_month = stoi(leaveAlice.substr(0, 2));
        int alice_leave_day = stoi(leaveAlice.substr(3, 2));

        int bob_arrived_month = stoi(arriveBob.substr(0, 2));
        int bob_arrived_day = stoi(arriveBob.substr(3, 2));
        int bob_leave_month = stoi(leaveBob.substr(0, 2));
        int bob_leave_day = stoi(leaveBob.substr(3, 2));

        unordered_map<int, int> mp = {
            {1, 31}, {2, 28}, {3, 31}, {4, 30},
            {5, 31}, {6, 30}, {7, 31}, {8, 31},
            {9, 30}, {10, 31}, {11, 30}, {12, 31}
        };

        int start_month = max(alice_arrived_month, bob_arrived_month);
        int start_day;

        if (alice_arrived_month == bob_arrived_month)
            start_day = max(alice_arrived_day, bob_arrived_day);
        else if (start_month == alice_arrived_month)
            start_day = alice_arrived_day;
        else
            start_day = bob_arrived_day;

        int end_month = min(alice_leave_month, bob_leave_month);
        int end_day;

        if (alice_leave_month == bob_leave_month)
            end_day = min(alice_leave_day, bob_leave_day);
        else if (end_month == alice_leave_month)
            end_day = alice_leave_day;
        else
            end_day = bob_leave_day;

        if (start_month > end_month ||
            (start_month == end_month && start_day > end_day))
            return 0;

        int total_days = 0;

        for (int i = start_month; i <= end_month; i++) {
            if (i == start_month && i == end_month)
                total_days += end_day - start_day + 1;
            else if (i == start_month)
                total_days += mp[i] - start_day + 1;
            else if (i == end_month)
                total_days += end_day;
            else
                total_days += mp[i];
        }

        return total_days;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis
- **Time Complexity:** \(O(1)\) — at most 12 months are processed.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(1)\) — the month-length map has a fixed size.
